{
  "Comment": "CloudLab c240g5, U11's worst case on Amazon 300M: the queries are 2M of the base's own vectors, drawn without repetition (scripts/data/sample_queries.py, seed 1), so no run repeats a query and none has any locality. They are drawn on the lab server, which has the index's layout map; their ground truth covers every 500th of the first 1M (fusion_gt --base). Otherwise experiment.amazon-300m-cloudlab-gpu-4to8-calibrate-4.json: the 4-node capacity, the nodes started on the 4-node warmup snapshot. The ladder reaches higher than there: drawn uniformly, the queries spread over the nodes as the data does, where the QAC searches put 1.67 times an even share on the busiest node.",
  "WorkDir": "/data-ssd/chenxu/work/amazon-300m",
